# Line endings are declared, not inherited from the operating system.
#
# The boot script becomes the instance user_data, and AWS compares its hash
# to decide whether to replace the instance. Without this file, an apply from
# Linux (LF) and another from Windows (CRLF) produce different hashes and the
# workstation is recreated for no real change.

*            text=auto eol=lf
*.tf         text eol=lf
*.tftpl      text eol=lf
*.hcl        text eol=lf
Jenkinsfile  text eol=lf
*.yml        text eol=lf
*.yaml       text eol=lf
Dockerfile   text eol=lf

# PowerShell run on Windows keeps its native line ending.
*.ps1        text eol=crlf

*.exe        binary
*.msi        binary
*.zip        binary
